; A STATIC MAP LEAVES NOTHING (maps.md §5.2).
; inputs: 1 2 5 9
; expect: 10 20 50 0
;
; `((map (1 10) (2 20) (5 50)) k)` is beta-tab with a SUM in the result
; position, and the `case` then folds against the constructor -- so no map, no
; tag, no allocation and no dispatch reach any backend. The normal form of the
; whole program is a constant.
;
; That is why F2 is affordable: free where it is used to THINK, priced where it
; is used to RUN. Absence is a RESULT rather than a stuck term, which is exactly
; where a map differs from an array -- an array's out-of-range index is left for
; the refinement layer to report, because its domain condition is discharged
; statically and a map's is discharged by the program.
(def run (fn (k)
  (case ((map (1 10) (2 20) (5 50)) k)
    (some v)  v
    none      0)))
